  "result": "The plan is written to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\add-a-new-parameter-playful-parasol.md`. The `ExitPlanMode` tool isn't available in this session, so I'm presenting it here for approval.\n\n**Plan for `click.KeyValue`**\n- **`src/click/types.py`**: add `class KeyValue(ParamType[tuple[str, str]])` after `UUIDParameterType`.\n  - It splits on the first `=` only, so `a=b=c` gives `('a', 'b=c')` and `a=` gives `('a', '')`.\n  - It fails via `self.fail` with `\"{value!r} is not a valid key=value pair.\"` when there is no `=` or the key is empty.\n  - It passes already-converted tuples through unchanged, as defaults need.\n- **`src/click/__init__.py`**: export `KeyValue`.\n- **Docs**: add an `autoclass` entry in `docs/api.md`, a bullet in `docs/parameter-types.md`, and a `CHANGES.md` entry. 8.5.0 is already released, so this needs a new unreleased section.\n- **Tests**: add parametrized cases in `tests/test_basic.py` for valid input, `a=b=c`, `a=`, `novalue` and `=v` (exit code 2 with the error message), and `multiple=True`. Also add an entry in `tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n- **Verification**: run `pytest`, plus a manual check with a small CLI using `--set`.\n\nApprove and I'll implement it (this needs plan mode to be exited), or tell me what to change.",
